  "definition": "Disclosures When Insurance is Required as a Condition of Obtaining a Loan",
  "effectiveDate": "1999-07-24",
  "historyNote": "#7064, eff 7-24-99",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Ins 3204.03",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 3204.03 Disclosures When Insurance is Required as a Condition of Obtaining a Loan",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3204.03 Disclosures When Insurance is Required as a Condition of Obtaining a Loan.\n\n(a) When a financial institution requires a customer to obtain insurance in connection with a loan the financial institution may inform customers that insurance is available from the financial institution, its subsidiary or an affiliate.\n\n(b) To avoid the impression that a connection exists between the financial institution’s credit decision and the customer’s choice of insurance seller, when insurance is available through the financial institution, a customer applying for a loan or an extension of credit shall be informed by the financial institution that:\n\n(1) The customer shall not be required to purchase insurance from the financial institution, a subsidiary or an affiliate; and,\n\n(2) The purchase of insurance from an agent of the customer’s choice shall not affect current or future credit decisions.\n\nSource. #7064, eff 7-24-99",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3200.html"
}
